        "q": "What are the steps to fact-check an article?",
        "a": "Mark every checkable claim, build a fact sheet listing each claim and its source, then check people and titles, quotes, numbers, dates, scientific claims, images and links against primary sources. Check what the piece implies as well as what it says. Resolve every open item with the writer and editor, and keep the fact sheet in case a claim is challenged after publication."
