        "a": "Not in the body of a story. Since 2014, AP spells out state names in text. It uses its own abbreviations, such as Calif. and Tenn., not postal codes, in datelines, photo captions, tables, lists and party affiliations. Alaska, Hawaii, Idaho, Iowa, Maine, Ohio, Texas and Utah are never abbreviated."
