        "a": "Studio and agency coverage usually runs two to five pages: a cover sheet with the title, writer, genre, page count and rating; a logline; a synopsis of one to two pages; and a page or so of comments. Paid development notes for writers can run longer, often five to ten pages, because they explain how to fix problems rather than only whether to read further."
