        "q": "How many slides should a 20-minute thesis defense have?",
        "a": "About 12 to 15 main slides, which works out at roughly 90 seconds per slide. Results slides usually need more time and the title slide less. Put extra detail on backup slides after the closing slide, so you can show them only if an examiner asks. Going over time is a worse mistake than having too few slides."
