        "a": "Usually yes, but not as it stands. Most publishers do not treat a thesis as prior publication: Elsevier says so explicitly, and Nature has said a doctoral thesis does not count as previously published. You still need to rewrite the work as a shorter article with one clear question, tell the editor it comes from your thesis, cite the thesis, and check the target journal's own policy."
